  "_notes": {
    "purpose": "COLD FILE case logic (authoring source of truth). Conforms to Case File Data Inventory v2.0 (the format authority). Prose lives in the single ink file named by meta.ink_file. Wholly fictional; any resemblance to real persons or events is unintended.",
    "prerequisites": "Every `prerequisites` / `unlock_rule` / `states[].when` is a FLAT array of fact IDs with AND semantics (null or [] = none). No expression DSL. OR is authored via the shared knowledge-fact idiom: each alternative route produces the SAME fact, gate on that fact — e.g. F-005 (warrant grounds) is emitted by both the Boyd interview (forged note) and the Rhonda motel interview (her slip), and the second-search actions gate on F-005. Time conditions use action.available (and blocks_of_day), never prereqs. 'Contradiction active' as a gate = list both of its facts; interview-side leverage stays in ink via contradictionActive().",
    "availability": "action.available = [from,to] absolute block range, inclusive; -1 = end of case; [0,-1] = always. Absolute block = day*blocks_per_day + block (0-based), so day 3 morning = block 9, day 5 morning = block 15. blocks_of_day is a periodic filter, e.g. [2] = evenings only.",
    "schedule": "Timed unprompted deliveries only (the sole survivor of the old trigger system). Everything the triggers used to do now lives at its effect site: unlocks in unlock_rule, action-enables in prerequisites, diorama changes in states[].when, delayed-result pagers in pending_label.",
    "inspect_and_reveal": "Inspectables are cost-0 INSPECT actions (one record type, one visibility system, one staging binding). hidden_reveal marks angle-only discovery; validator law: never the sole route to a critical fact (A-14 reveals F-010, but A-11 also produces it).",
    "decoy_pool_tokens": "reconstruction slot decoy_pool = an explicit ID list OR a token: discovered_persons | discovered_places | discovered_vehicles | discovered_objects | discovered_times.",
    "ink_contract": "external fns available to ink: hasFact(id), contradictionActive(id), discoverFact(id), day(), spendBlock(). Interview fact_manifest must be a superset of the knot's discoverFact() calls (validator cross-check).",
    "underscore_keys": "Any key beginning with `_` is an authoring annotation, stripped by the compiler and ignored by the validator."
  },

